-- title:
--   Image of P⁰ in J_H[p]: cyclotomic inertia part, finite
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be an odd prime and $M$ a non-zero natural number with $p \mid M$ and $p^{2} \nmid M$, and let $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ contain every unit whose image under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times} \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$ is $1$; let $S$ be a set of naturals and assume [`ModularCurve.HeckeDiamondInputsHAll M H`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L113), i.e. the Hecke input data at level $H$ along every prime together with, for each $d$, a diamond automorphism of the base-changed function field of $X_H(M)$. Write $J = J_H(M)$ for $\mathrm{Pic}^0$ of that function field over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ and $T = T_p J$ for the group of sequences $(x_n)$ in $J$ with $p^{n}x_n = 0$ and $p\,x_{n+1} = x_n$. Let $\mathbb{T}$ be a commutative $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra acting on $T$ compatibly with the $\mathbb{Z}_p$-structure, faithfully (only $0$ annihilates all of $T$), together with a map `op` from the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_q$ ($q \mid M$) and $\langle d \rangle$ to $\mathbb{T}$ acting as the corresponding endomorphisms [`ModularCurve.tateGenOpH`](def/ModularCurve_XHOperators.html#L99) of $T$, whose image generates $\mathbb{T}$ as a $\mathbb{Z}_p$-algebra. Let $S'$ be an idempotent splitting of $\mathbb{T}$: a finite family of complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ and of maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ exactly when $i \neq j$; fix an index $i_0$ with $\mathrm{op}(U_p) \notin \mathfrak{m}_{i_0}$, and write $P = e_{i_0}T$ for the corner submodule. Let $\mathfrak{P}$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a non-unit, with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, and let $I$ be its inertia subgroup in $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$, $\varepsilon$ the $p$-adic cyclotomic character. Let $P^0 \subseteq T$ be a $\mathbb{T}$-submodule characterised by $x \in P^0$ iff $x \in P$ and $\sigma x = \varepsilon(\sigma)x$ for all $\sigma \in I$. Let $\Lambda$ be level data at $\mathfrak{P}$ and $O$ a Néron object [`ModularCurve.JHNeronObjectAtP`](def/ModularCurve_JHNeronObjectAtP.html#L53) for it, with finite-part subgroups $O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m \le J$ generated by the $m$-torsion classes whose point over the generic point extends over $\mathfrak{P}$. Assume (i) for every $m > 0$, every $\sigma \in I$ and every $m$-torsion class $x$, one has $\sigma x - x \in O.\mathrm{finPts}\,m$, and (ii) for all $\sigma, \sigma' \in I$ and $x \in P$, $\sigma'(\sigma x - x) = \varepsilon(\sigma')(\sigma x - x)$. Then, denoting by $\overline{(\cdot)}$ the image under the first-coordinate projection $T \to J$, $\bar x \in \overline{P^0}$ holds if and only if $\bar x \in \overline{P}$ and for every $\sigma \in I$ and every natural number $c$ such that $\sigma\zeta = \zeta^{c}$ for all $p$-th roots of unity $\zeta$ one has $\sigma \bar x = c\,\bar x$; and moreover $\overline{P^0} \le O.\mathrm{finPts}\,p$.
--
--   This is the Tate–SGA 7 half of the Galois-theoretic analysis of the ordinary corner at $p$: the mod $p$ image of the cyclotomic-inertia part of $e_{i_0}T_pJ_H(M)$ is cut out inside $\overline{e_{i_0}T_pJ_H(M)}$ by the same inertia condition read on $p$-torsion, and consists of points in the finite part of the Néron object at $\mathfrak{P}$. It feeds the construction of the injective map identifying a multiplicative submodule with the dual of the space of polarised regular differentials at level $H$.
